BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Arts Guild of Sonoma Presents: California Gold
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T170700
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T193000
UID:260627J_d9owClPEWCWT0_HoEJlg
DESCRIPTION:Discover *California Gold*\, a special exhibition at the Arts 
 Guild of Sonoma featuring work of selected member artworks celebrating Cal
 ifornia landscapes and lifestyle. Celebrate the US 250th anniversary with 
 member Jackie Lee’s painting featuring the Grand Canyon paired with an A
 merican eagle in flight. See the vibrant abstract paintings of Sonoma gues
 t artist Carola McAndrew. Terri Heartfire is the July Featured Guild Artis
 t\, presenting her colorful glass works. it's all happening this July 1 
 – August 3 at the Arts Guild of Sonoma. Join us for a free public recept
 ion during Sonoma Art Walk on Thursday\, July 2\, from 5 to 7:30 p.m.\, at
  140 East Napa Street in Sonoma. The Arts Guild of Sonoma is one of the lo
 ngest running art collectives in California and features original painting
 s\, jewelry\, sculpture\, photography\, ceramics\, and gift items by local
  original artists. The gallery is open Wednesday through Monday\, 11 a.m. 
 to 5 p.m. Public welcome.
LOCATION:Arts Guild of Sonoma
URL:https://artsguildofsonoma.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:James Kelly (of Redwood Chrome) + Juke Tannins
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T193000
UID:260626xjn_LJdTpkuC9lcBWacU6Q
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird23 at checkout. Offer ends June 28th.\n\nPromo C
 odes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\, b
 ut must be typed as one word.\n\nAn intimate set of astral infused folk. I
 f Townes Van Zandt vacationed on Mars\, it may have ended up sounding a bi
 t like James Kelly on his days off from the raucous sets of Redwood Chro
 me.  A night of introspection and sonic exploration await.\n\nhttps://www
 .instagram.com/redwoodchromeband https://youtu.be/WvXs\\_ZDg3-4\n\nhttps:/
 /redwoodchrome.com/\n\nJuke Tannins is what happens when you take a vetera
 n East Coast musician\, arm him with a curated vault of American music\, a
 nd drop him in the middle of Wine Country. Juke specializes in curating th
 e perfect soundtrack for the moment. He treats the setlist like a wine pai
 ring: serving up exactly what the audience needs\, right when they need it
 .\n\nA bonus pairing of Juke \\+ James will also be on the tasting menu.\n
 \nhttps://juketannins.com/bio https://www.instagram.com/theejuketannins Re
 commended If You Like: Michael Hurley\, John Prine\, and Daniel Johnston
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 00009ZNHVMA4
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kathleen Alexander Artist Exhibition & Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T180000
UID:260626X9SCK_jne0ec9RhR5JZqFg
DESCRIPTION:In Coastal Currents\, Sea Ranch artist Kathleen Alexander pres
 ents paintings inspired by the rugged Northern California coast. Her work 
 honors the species that inhabit this landscape while acknowledging their r
 esilience and vulnerability. After spending the first 45 years of her life
  in the Bay Area\, Alexander moved to Maui for twelve years where tropical
  flowers were the focus of her paintings. After moving back to California\
 , Alexander found new sources of inspiration in her backyard along our bea
 utiful coast. The abalone shells recall a once-thriving coastal tradition\
 , no longer allowed due to habitat loss and declining populations. Pelican
 s in flight capture the quiet strength of these iconic birds. Kelp paintin
 gs\, created with permission from underwater photographer and filmmaker Ma
 rco Mazza\, reveal the underwater forests that sustain marine life. Alexan
 der’s plein air oil paintings capture a moment in time along the coast. 
 Through her paintings\, Kathleen Alexander invites reflection on what endu
 res—and what we are called to protect—along this remarkable coast.\n\n
 www.KathleenAlexanderArt.com\n\nwww.GreyWhaleGallery.com\n\nIG: @kathleena
 lexanderart\n\nSubmitted June 24th 2026
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
