BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T210000
UID:260617mUSsQS3FU0a8x8HKLQCanw
DESCRIPTION:A Southern debutante shares a body with a gay New Yorker—com
 ic chaos meets Provincetown magic. When Southern debutante Miss Magnolia B
 eatrice Devareux Beaumont chokes on a pork rib\, she awakens in the body o
 f a middle-aged\, gay New Yorker—“Master Joseph”—en route to Provi
 ncetown for a birthday getaway. What begins as shock and spirited disagree
 ment turns into an unexpected journey of shared consciousness\, clashing p
 erspectives\, and surprising tenderness. More than a monologue\, Miss Magn
 olia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown is a witty\, heartfelt solo play explor
 ing identity\, purpose\, and the magic of Provincetown. Hailed as “rich\
 , wise\, and deeply human” \\(Backstage\\) and “a fierce and funny fab
 le” \\(Next Magazine\\)\, this charming comic fantasy celebrates the bea
 uty of unlikely connection. Learn more about Joe and the show on Instagram
  https://www.instagram.com/joehutcheson/ TICKETS: PURCHASE IN ADVANCE AND 
 SAVE! Zones A & B ensure a seat. Zone C has limited seating\, plus standin
 g room. Zone A  $30 Zone B $25 Zone C $20 \\(does not guarantee seating\\)
  Tickets at the door $30 \\(Zone C only\\) Doors open 6:30pm.  Our kitchen
  serves our All New Menu from the time doors open until end of intermissio
 n. \\(Kitchen available only at events with 60 or more advance tickets sol
 d\\)
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1023509423669806/1023510573669691/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
