BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3rd of July Fireworks & Music Extravaganza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T220000
UID:260624nYO6V01QxEuXbpZzPDrHiQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day the West County way at the 53rd Ann
 ual Sebastopol Kiwanis 3rd of July Fireworks & Music Extravaganza on Frida
 y\, July 3\, 2026. This beloved hometown tradition returns bigger and bett
 er at the Sebastopol Community Cultural Center — bringing together thous
 ands of locals and visitors for an unforgettable evening of music\, food\,
  fun\, and fireworks. The festivities kick off at 4:00 PM with live music 
 on three stages featuring Contigo\, The Musers\, The New Sky Band\, and a 
 DJ after-party. Stroll the grounds for delicious food trucks\, a full beer
  and wine garden\, and the popular Kid’s Corner with games\, a bounce ho
 use\, dunk tank\, and family-friendly activities. Kids of all ages will lo
 ve the festive atmosphere as the sun sets over the scenic West Sonoma Coun
 ty hills. Premium Seating is available inside the Community Cultural Cente
 r with special perks and parking. As darkness falls\, the sky lights up wi
 th a spectacular professional fireworks display launched at approximately 
 9:30 PM. This dazzling show has been a cherished Sonoma County tradition f
 or more than five decades\, presented by the Kiwanis Club of Sebastopol. A
 ll proceeds support the Kiwanis Club’s mission to fund local scholarship
 s\, youth programs\, and community service projects throughout Sebastopol 
 and beyond. Bring your blankets\, lawn chairs\, and the whole family for a
  safe\, festive\, and patriotic night that truly captures the spirit of co
 mmunity and celebration.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://www.sebastopolkiwanisclub.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friday Night Comedy - Danielle Arce & Nick Larson - Downtown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T220000
UID:2606249wAGBN9XG0uyBwM3yJY2gQ
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TAB
 LES NOW AVAILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own pr
 ivate call button to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (
 or a bottle of wine) for only $95!\n\nEvery Friday night hilarious comedia
 ns from The Bay Area and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick arou
 nd after for late-night karaoke! Fresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThi
 s Week: Jon Lehre (host) Hayden Remi Headliners: Nick Larson & Danielle La
 rson\n\nDanielle Arce started stand-up comedy in 2011\, and has since perf
 ormed all over the country and overseas! She was featured on To Tell the T
 ruth on ABC & Hulu in 2021\, and has performed for the US Troops (Navy & M
 arines) in Japan. She's also performed in Australia\, and in festivals all
  over the country including New York City\, Phoenix\, and more. She's the 
 co-host of the Secret Minorities Podcast and is known for her quick\, dark
  & witty humor.\n\nNick Larson is an experienced\, Latino comedian from St
 ockton\, California. He has performed all over the US\, and regularly head
 lines and features at clubs and venues all along the West coast & Pacific 
 Northwest. Nick has been performing since 2012\, and is known for his goof
 y and silly sense of humor\, mining his unique family life for most of his
  comedy gold. He is also known for his hilarious riffing and crowd work\, 
 while seamlessly weaving it into his prepared material. He is a co-host fo
 r two popular comedy podcasts\, including "Joke Me Off Podcast" with fello
 w Latino comedian\, Saul Trujillo\, and "Secret Minorities" with Latina co
 median\, Danielle Arce. Nick has been interviewed and featured for Comedy 
 Network Live and has won many comedy competitions in The Bay Area and Cent
 ral Valley.\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **
 wwww.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/friday-night-comedy-danielle-arce-nick-la
 rson-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1990246979291
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SCREAM at Fun Size Blasted Art Gallery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T200000
UID:2606240Ig-fzwEVUGqbLTf39ga0w
DESCRIPTION:Twelve Sonoma County artists will “SCREAM” together in a m
 iniature exhibit. The exhibit\, as well as every individual artwork in the
  show share the same title: SCREAM.\n\nThe miniature FUN SIZE Blasted Art 
 Gallery\, which measures 16 x 33 x 21”\, serves as a portable vessel for
  this chorus of artists\, was created as a timely response to global\, nat
 ional\, local\, and personal issues.\n\nThese artists will be SCREAMing to
 gether: Arminée Chahbazian\, Art Moura\, Bill Shelley\, Britta Kathmeyer\
 , Carlos Perez\, Chris Beards\, Jennifer Mygatt Tatum\, Kathleen Youngquis
 t\, Keviette Minor\, Kristen Throop\, Nick Mancillas\, and Nicole Mathers.
 \n\nThe Friday\, July 3\, Opening Reception is at the Santa Rosa Arts Cent
 er in the SOFA Arts District (312 South A Street\, Santa Rosa) at 5-8pm\, 
 coinciding with SOFA Arts District First Friday.  \n\nAlso see SCREAM on
  Saturday\, July 11\, at Studio LZ Gallery in The Watershed\, (429 First S
 treet\, Suite 130\, Petaluma) at 4-6pm.\n\nSCREAM and FUN SIZE Blasted Art
  Gallery are a project of Blasted Art Gallery (Santa Rosa artists Chris Be
 ards & Bill Shelley)\, which presented gallery exhibits featuring Sonoma C
 ounty artists from 2017 to 2019 in the SOFA Arts District in Santa Rosa\, 
 and online in 2020.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Arts Center
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/scream-at-fun-size-blas
 ted-art-gallery/19154813/2026-07-03T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
