BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fourth of July Night Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T230000
UID:260607Yi5jqE_8g0m8VVNq995aSw
DESCRIPTION:Join Team Sugarloaf and Sonoma Ecology Center and clim
 b one of the tallest mountains in Sonoma Valley—Bald Mountainan
 d enjoy a spectacular vantage point to view as many as 16 diff
 erent fireworks displays! This strenuous hike covers approximately
  6.5 miles roundtrip with over 1500 ft. elevation gain\, includi
 ng steep sections. Expect approximately 1.5 hours hiking time eac
 h way. \n\nUpon arrival at the top of Bald Mountain\, you’ll 
 enjoy a mountaintop reception: hearty snacks and sweets\, refreshi
 ng lemonade\, and water. Kick back\, relax\, and enjoy the beaut
 iful sights of fireworks displays that span the Bay Area—from 
 Windsor in the north\, Berkeley and Oakland in the east\, and S
 an Francisco to the south\, with possible views into the South 
 Bay.\n\nSpace is limited for this annual event\, and we expect t
 o sell out. Reserve your space now! Tickets are $80 for general
  audiences\, $40 for students\, youth \\(12-17 year olds\\)\, and
  Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers. Youth must be accompanied by a pa
 rent or legal guardian. This event is not recommended for childr
 en under 12 years old.\n\nProceeds support Sonoma Ecology Center
 ’s operations of Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. We have tax-deduct
 ible sponsorships available to defray the costs. Each sponsorship
  includes one ticket to the event.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/4thofjuly2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T170000
UID:260529nBjiHqEYy0Wz1BCb9yVx2A
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T160000
UID:260523317DjPyv60yL6i28xNipeA
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\n**Lavender Bloom Fest Field Days:*
 * May 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\n**Lavender Su
 nset Evenings:** May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\n**Jaz
 z Days:** May 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\n**Lavender U-Cut Experience:*
 * June 27-28\, July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, bu
 t is listed under Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\
 , play farm bingo\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop t
 he Farm Stand and visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are spe
 cial at Bees N Blooms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on
  the lavender. Enjoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrin
 th to watch the sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seaweed Foraging (Sonoma Coast) in Bodega Bay
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T120000
UID:260522k0AxT0zqVkKKHvtk2bpexg
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to identify\, use\, and sustainably harvest the bou
 ntiful seaweeds. Harvest up to 10 lbs of seaweed to take home and enjoy. 
 \n\nFrom ancient times to the present\, seaweeds have been used by coastal
  people all over the world to nourish themselves and their gardens\, as w
 ell as for health issues. The Sonoma coast is incredibly rich in seaweeds
  that can be used as food and medicine. \n\nWe will gather on the beach\
 , review some common edible species\, and head to where the sea meets sho
 re to access and appreciate the abundant marine meadow growing on our coas
 t.\n\nThe class also includes community-building activities and will concl
 ude with a cooking demo featuring several varieties of seaweed.  Led by A
 utumn Summers and Ricardo Romero Gianoli\n\nClass Dates (not a series)\n\n
 Fri 6/5 8 am\n\nSat 6/6 8:45 am\n\nFri 6/19 8:15 am\n\nSat 6/20 8:45 am\n\
 nMore dates available in July
LOCATION:Bodega Bay
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/seaweed-foraging-sonoma-coast-in-bodega-b
 ay/2026-06-05/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
