BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T170000
UID:260508HiTfkeimh0ewXsZN-oDsUg
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Restorative Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T113000
UID:260427i0y3d_Sq1ECfbP8HG_o_AQ
DESCRIPTION:Begin your summer Saturday mornings with a calming session of 
 restorative yoga at the Garden - an invitation to slow down\, breathe deep
 ly\, and reconnect with yourself in a peaceful natural setting. Whether yo
 u’re looking to unwind from a busy week or manage ongoing stress\, this 
 beginner-friendly class offers a gentle path toward physical and emotional
  balance. Join us to explore the deeply relaxing practices of Yoga Nidra\,
  Yin Yoga\, and restorative postures—all designed to release tension\, c
 alm the nervous system\, and support mindful rest. Classes take place indo
 ors in our Center for Learning & Engagement\, surrounded by the peaceful e
 nergy of the Garden\, it’s the perfect setting to unwind. Sessions are l
 ed by our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, who special
 ize in making yoga both accessible and engaging. These sessions are led by
  our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, a community-cent
 ered studio with over 20 years of experience and a dynamic team of yoga\, 
 fitness\, and meditation guides to support your practice. Please dress acc
 ordingly and bring water.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. Stella Heath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T180000
UID:260206jODiZ1tawkKmVwbIyCTzTg
DESCRIPTION:*Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come 
 together.*\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a ta
 sting room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acr
 oss the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll 
 and Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new so
