BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: The Hidden Truth About Death in Custody
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260709T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260709T200000
UID:260630Syjq9Nyx4kmZW0adzRjh_A
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation with acclaimed author and UCLA Prof
 essor Terence Keel on how autopsy reports mask the truth about in-custod
 y deaths\, which disproportionately involve Black and Latino men.\n\nEach 
 year\, police officers kill over 1\,000 people they’ve sworn to protect 
 and serve. While some cases\, like George Floyd’s and Sandra Bland’s\,
  capture national attention\, most victims remain nameless\, their stories
  untold. In *The Coroner’s Silence: Death Records and the Hidden Victim
 s of Police Violence*\, Dr. Keel reveals a disturbing fact: Coroners and m
 edical examiners often omit key information about police actions\, attribu
 ting deaths to preexisting health conditions or victims’ own actions.\n\
 nEmail racialjusticeallies@gmail.com to register.
LOCATION:Zoom
URL:http://www.racialjusticeallies.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
