 ys as a grower—including how his unique connections to the Grateful Dead
  inspired his path—and discussing the evolution of Sonoma’s organic an
 d biodynamic wine movement. He’ll also share his thoughts on the state o
 f the wine industry today.\n\nWhether you're a backyard grower\, a passion
 ate hobbyist\, professional winemaker\, or just love a great Sonoma wine s
 tory\, you won't want to miss this lively discussion with the "Godfather o
 f Sonoma Wine Country" -- in the Secret Garden at the Sonoma Community Cen
 ter.\n\n📅 **When:** Thursday\, July 9th at 6:30-8:00\, Doors Open 6:
 30 PM | Talk 7:00 PM - 8:00PM\n\n📍 **Where:** Sonoma Community Center
 \, outside in the Secret Garden \n\n🎟️ **RSVP:** Head over to the 
 Sonoma Index-Tribune events calendar or visit \\[Insert Website Link\\] fo
 r full event details!\n\n**Note:**  21+ only| Bring a glass for tasting 
 and if you're a home winemaker a bottle to share\n\n**Cost:** Free\n\n**W
 ebsite:** sonomahomewine.org/calendar
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center - Outside in the Secret Garden
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1991078118250?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
