BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chef and Top Chef Alum Chef Nelson German Celebrates Debut Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T170000
UID:260630bmWGBb4mUEqNFNBZIH1Oaw
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to join us for an exclusive culinary experienc
 e on July 11\, 2026 in the heart of Sonoma's wine country to celebrate the
  upcoming book release "Caribbean Cocktails: Drinks & Bites from the Afro
 -Latino Diaspora"\, \\(June 2\, 2026 from Ten Speed Press\\). The book is 
 authored by chef and cocktail creator Nelson German and James Beard Awar
 d–winning culinary writer Andréa Lawson Gray.\n\nHosted by PREMO Club 
 at Aldina Vineyards' tasting lounge at Bacchus Landing\, the gathering wil
 l feature cocktails\, wine\, an author conversation\, book signing\, and d
 inner experience\, with net proceeds benefiting Sprouts Chef Training\, a 
 nonprofit organization that empowers youth through culinary education.\n\n
 The event begins at 3 pm with a wine and cheese reception featuring canap
 és and cocktails from the book. The authors will be joined by special gue
 st LJ Maingard of Little Saint Farm as they engage in a conversation explo
 ring how herbs\, spices\, fruits\, and aromatic plants connect the Caribbe
 an\, Africa\, and California through histories of migration\, cultivation\
 , and exchange.\n\nThe evening continues at 5pm with a second cocktail rec
 eption featuring herbs\, fruits\, and botanicals grown at Little Saint Far
 m\, followed by an intimate multi-course tasting dinner highlighting the f
 arm’s seasonal produce. The evening concludes with dessert under the sta
 rs.\n\nVisit https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
  to purchase tickets and for more info.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
