BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Marcus & Devin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T143000
UID:260608MRzRufcPTkGS3kbQCRy5og
DESCRIPTION:Unplug and Groove: P-Butta Live at the Vineyard\n\nJoin us for
  No Cell Sundays with P-Butta\, a local powerhouse trio that's been making
  Sonoma County move for decades.\n\nP-Butta is the instrumental side proje
 ct of the musicians from Rising Tide\, the original Groundation band. With
  Marcus Urani on keyboards\, Ryan Newman on bass\, and Paul Spina on drums
 \, this three-piece brings together four decades of funk\, soul\, and jazz
  mastery that satisfies any musical palate.\n\nExpect to hear groovy cover
 s from legendary artists like The Meters\, Booker T & the M.G.'s\, Herbie 
 Hancock\, Donnie Hathaway\, Cannonball Adderley\, and even the Beastie Boy
 s. Whether you're a jazz head or just love good vibes\, P-Butta delivers t
 he perfect soundtrack for a Sunday afternoon in wine country.\n\nWhat's No
  Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, reconnect wi
 th great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Check your phone 
 with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Bring a blanket\
 , grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-p-butta
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival Concert 2: With Love From Vienna
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
UID:260606uSX5xtTvXU2QiA5SLndaow
DESCRIPTION:Travel to 19th-century Vienna for an afternoon of chamber musi
 c. From the lush German Romanticism of Mendelssohn and Brahms to the wistf
 ul Slavic dances of Chopin and Dvořák\, the program also spotlights Math
 ilde Kralik\, a compelling voice waiting to be rediscovered. Guests are in
 vited to stay afterward for a wine reception and conversation. Approximate
 ly 2 hours with intermission.\n\nThe Valley of the Moon Music Festival ret
 urns July 11–26\, 2026\, with Postcards from Dvořák\, a season inspire
 d by the travels\, influences\, and cultural connections behind the compos
 er’s music. Set in the heart of Sonoma Valley\, the festival brings toge
 ther internationally acclaimed musicians for historically informed perform
 ances that blend world-class classical music with the beauty and charm of 
 wine country.
LOCATION:Hanna Center Auditorium
URL:https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.org/event/with-love-from-vienna/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T170000
UID:260529GRHzwtbtzUqkr4bUv7d5Dw
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plot Twists & Pinot: A Summer Bookish Afternoon in Sonoma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T150000
UID:2605262_qNm2PW1kqkPTavOfZ_5A
DESCRIPTION:Some Sundays are just Sundays. This one's going to be differen
 t.\n\nPlot Twists & Pinot is a wine country afternoon for people who love 
 books\, a great beverage\, and would love to spend a few hours with others
  who feel the same way. Hosted by Novel Pairings at Sangiacomo Family Wine
 s in Sonoma \\(one of wine country's most beloved family estates\, farming
  this land since 1927\\) it's the kind of afternoon that's genuinely hard 
 to find and easy to love.\n\nHere's what you're actually signing up for: a
  welcome pour\, two rounds of bookish trivia with trope-based teams\, a ga
 me where you try to figure out whether a dramatic description is talking a
 bout a wine or a romance novel love interest \\(harder than it sounds\\)\,
  Badly Explained Books\, a community book swap where you bring a favorite 
 and leave with something you never would have found on your own\, vineyard
  lounge areas to settle into\, and a local food truck. All of it outside\,
  in a Sonoma vineyard\, on a July Sunday.\n\nJoin 75 people who love book
 s and wine\, an afternoon designed to feel effortless\, and a host who mak
 es sure everyone feels at home from the moment they arrive. \n\nSolo atte
 ndees are more than welcome! Our host facilitates introductions throughout
  the afternoon so you won't spend a single minute wondering what to do nex
 t. This is the event you've been waiting for someone to throw. We threw it
 .\n\nEarly bird tickets: $25 general admission / $15 members through June 
 26.\n\nStandard pricing: $35 general admission / $25 members.
LOCATION:Sangiacomo Family Wines
URL:https://www.novel-pairings.com/plottwists
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
UID:260523iy3XgYLNGkiKhxRzfWpy8g
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\n**Lavender Bloom Fest Field Days:*
 * May 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\n**Lavender Su
 nset Evenings:** May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\n**Jaz
 z Days:** May 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\n**Lavender U-Cut Experience:*
 * June 27-28\, July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, bu
 t is listed under Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\
 , play farm bingo\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop t
 he Farm Stand and visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are spe
 cial at Bees N Blooms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on
  the lavender. Enjoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrin
 th to watch the sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
