BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thai Cooking Class Benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T193000
UID:2604251FkuuFpqK0GUcMCd0da3Uw
DESCRIPTION:Thai Cooking Class with Chef Kanyaa & Tina - July 16\n\n$125.0
 0\n\nJoin Sonoma Family Meal's very own Chef Kanyaa and recent culinary tr
 aining graduate Tina for a unique Thai cooking class featuring favorites f
 rom their homeland. Kanyaa brings her culinary experience and heritage fro
 m the Northeastern Thai region of Isaan\, which is specifically known for 
 it's delectable cuisine and Tina\, also a Thai-born cook\, brings her pass
 ion for food systems and her newfound skills and confidence from the CJT p
 rogram to share with you all.\n\nIn this hands-on two hour class\, you wil
 l learn the breakdown of how to make several traditional Thai specialties 
 and receive the recipes and cooking instructions to take home. You will wo
 rk in teams to prepare all the food under Chef's guidance\, and then enjoy
  the meal together family style at the end!\n\nWHEN: Thursday July 16\, 5-
 7:30pm WHERE: SFM community kitchen\, 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nPLEA
 SE WEAR CLOSE TOED SHOES TO ALL CLASSES\n\nTHE MENU:\n\nVegetable Fresh Sp
 ring Rolls\n\nChicken Khao Soi \\(Northern Thai Curry Noodle Soup\\)\n\nVe
 getable Pad Thai with Tofu\n\nMango Ube Sticky Rice\n\nIf you have a speci
 fic food allergy or have any questions about the menu\, please contact han
 nah@sonomafamilymeal.org.\n\nHear it from our customers:\n\n"Kudos to Chef
  Kanyaa!  We loved the Thai Chicken Curry last night. Cooked perfectly\,
  it was delicious! The egg rolls and dipping sauce so yummy\, I could eat
  those every night." - Karyl\n\nAbout Tina:\n\nYaowalak “Tina” is a Th
 ai-born cook and former nonprofit professional who studied food systems an
 d worked in environmental and community-focused organizations in Thailand.
  Now\, drawing on her family’s market cooking roots and her passion for 
 food\, is building the skills and confidence through Sonoma Family Meal’
 s culinary training program to launch her own business in private cheffing
  and cooking education.\n\nAbout Kanyaa:\n\nOriginally from the Isan regio
 n of Thailand\, Kanyaa is a passionate cook with experience in pastry and 
 much more. She lives in Rohnert Park with her teen son\, and in her free t
 ime\, enjoys preparing the dishes of her homeland\, like chicken over rice
  and noodle soup. As the kitchen assistant\, Kanyaa assists with the kitch
 en’s day-to-day operations\, her favorite part of the role is "cooking f
 or the community."\n\nQuan
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/store-2/thaicooking
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GREG SARRIS AND REBECCA SOLNIT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T200000
UID:260424DDR_yqhi_0SphuL4Eoj4LQ
DESCRIPTION:SANTA ROSA --\n\nCopperfield’s Books is deeply honored to we
 lcome Greg Sarris home to Santa Rosa for a preeminent evening celebrating 
 his powerful new novel\, *The Last Human Bear*.\n\nChairman of the Federa
 ted Indians of Graton Rancheria and one of Sonoma County’s most revered 
 literary voices\, Mr. Sarris will be joined in conversation by acclaimed a
 uthor Rebecca Solnit\, renowned for her work in climate and human rights a
 dvocacy.\n\nThis special event is free and open to the public and will tak
 e place at the Finley Community Center -- bringing together community\, st
 ory\, and a rare literary homecoming.\n\nDoors open at 6:30pm. *Registrat
 ion strongly encouraged due to strict venue capacity limits.*\n\n**"It's r
 evelatory on every page." --Dave Eggers**\n\n**"The grand return of a mast
 er storyteller." --Peter Maravelis\, City Lights Booksellers**\n\n**An epi
 c story of curses\, love\, hard-won independence\, and healing--and the fi
 rst novel in 28 years by a widely acclaimed Native writer.**\n\nMary Hatch
 er lives with a curse--or is it a power that could make her life whole? A 
 Native Pomo woman who comes of age in 1930s California\, Mary keeps trying
  to make sense of her enigmatic family. Strange rumors spread about her. H
 er stepmother may have taught her how to become a Human Bear\, a shapeshif
 ter who can menace and poison enemies. Two men may love her--or love who t
 hey think she is. A mystery even to herself\, Mary learns to pass between 
 Native and white societies\, tenaciously carving her own path as an indepe
 ndent woman. But as she explores love and desire\, family inherited and ch
 osen\, and the secrets of the natural world\, one question gnaws at her: I
 s she fated to do harm?\n\nWry and richly lyrical\, *The Last Human Bear*
  follows Mary from the Great Depression to the twenty-first century\, whe
 n she commits a haunting final act. Inspired by the Native women elders wh
 o shaped Greg Sarris in his youth\, it is the triumphant and revelatory re
 turn of an eminent novelist. With illustrations by Obi Kaufmann.\n\n**Auth
 or:**\n\n**Greg Sarris** is an enrolled member of the Federated Indians of
  Graton Rancheria and is currently serving his seventeenth consecutive ele
 cted term as chairman of the tribe. He is the author of several books\, in
 cluding the novel *Grand Avenue*\, which he adapted for an HBO miniseries
  and co-executive produced with Robert Redford\; the novel *Watermelon Ni
 ghts*\; *Weaving the Dream*\, a biography of Mabel McKay\; *Becoming Sto
 ry*\, a memoir\; and the story collections *How a Mountain Was Made* and
  *The Forgetters*. Formerly a full professor of English at UCLA\, Sarris 
 serves on the University of California Board of Regents and the Sundance I
 nstitute Board\, and he holds the Distinguished Emeritus Graton Endowed Ch
 air in Native American Studies at Sonoma State University. He lives in Son
 oma County\, California.\n\n**Rebecca Solnit** is the author of more than
  25 books\, including *Orwell's Roses*\, *Hope in the Dark*\, *Men Expl
 ain Things to Me*\, *A Paradise Built in Hell: The Extraordinary Communit
 ies That Arise in Disaster*\, and *A Field Guide to Getting Lost*. A long
 time climate and human rights activist\, she serves on the boards of Oil C
 hange International and Third Act. Her newsletter of essays and analyses c
 an be found at meditationsinanemergency.com.\n\n**Praise:**\n\n"*The Last
  Human Bear* is a very complex\, very moving meditation on personal origi
 ns and family lore\, illuminating a part of California's history that's ra
 rely seen in literature. It's revelatory on every page." --**Dave Eggers**
 \, author of *A Heartbreaking Work of Staggering Genius*\n\n"A page into
  *The Last Human Bear*\, Greg Sarris writes\, 'The heart has no limits.' 
 Thus begins an exploration of the heart--its longings\, aches\, grievances
 \, regrets\, hates\, and loves. Sarris has given us a love letter to the w
 estern landscape and the people who call it home." --**Lisa See**\, author
  of *Daughters of the Sun and Moon* and *Lady Tan's Circle of Women*\n\
 n"*The Last Human Bear* is a love story\, a tale of place and of a bold-v
 oiced woman whose life has been misunderstood\, and a vaulting American ya
 rn that carries you along like a leaf on the wind." --**John Freeman**\, a
 uthor of *California Rewritten*\n\n"The novel traces the very long life o
 f one Pomo woman\, from the 1930s to the present\, and the breathtaking ch
 anges of that span: to nature\, the built environment\, social ties\, and 
 traditional ways. It asks and answers critical questions and implicates th
 e reader in that conversation\, telling a remarkable twisting story along 
 the way. This novel is literally unforgettable: it will embed itself in yo
 ur mind and stay there." --**Christie Olson Day\, Gallery Bookshop**
LOCATION:Finley Community Center
URL:https://SARRIS_SOLNIT_SANTAROSA.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T193000
UID:260415o6lmv78OtEiVx1rznh6_0w
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Windsor Summer Nights on the Green
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T000000
UID:260327z0TgQyuy2Uy9nP1XpYiw9Q
DESCRIPTION:Freestone Peaches\, based out of the SF Bay Area\, emulates th
 e feel\, excitement and energy of the Allman Brothers Band during their va
 rious eras from Duane to Derek. The band brings the raw energy and full th
