BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Local Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T180000
UID:260616AEGkgy3oOEyDKVbam3FSUQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  6/15/26\n\n**JULY EXHIBIT: LOC
 AL COLOR**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 29 – July 26\, 2026**\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, July 4\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Linda Barretta  
 and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  
 Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beaut
 iful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Linda Barretta** presents **Local Color\,** a collecti
 on unveiling new oil paintings that tap into the vivid natural hues found 
 in our region’s breathtaking beauty.  From flowers to vineyards\, colo
 r takes a starring role in these works.  The deep purple hills in “Sun
 flower Daze” intensify the golden sweep of the sunflowers.  A peach tr
 ee celebrates the season with a glorious pink floral display in “Spring 
 Blooms.”  In “Winery Farm and Gardens\,” framed through a natural 
 arch of trees\, a sunlit vineyard draws the viewer.  “We are so fortun
 ate to live in Sonoma wine country – it’s stunning beauty is a daily i
 nspiration to pick up my brushes and paint\,” commented Barretta. \n\nL
 iving in Healdsburg\, Sonoma wine country is Barretta’s homebase.  She
  developed her impressionist style and skills through numerous hours of pl
 ein air painting and studying with master artists.  When Barretta create
 s the composition\, she is observing the play of light and colors that wil
 l highlight the compelling quality of the scene.  Her aim is to translat
 e her inspiration to the viewer.  From the rough sketch to the final bru
 shstroke\, this is the task she loves.  Barretta participates in the Art
  Trails Open Studio program and her works are exhibited regionally and thr
 oughout the country\,\n\nMeet the artist: Barretta will host the Gallery o
 n July 4\, 6 & 26\, 2:30 – 6pm and July 22\, 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\nThe Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Beverly Bird’s Birds by Bird\,** a
  collection of acrylic paintings that depict our feathered friends\, big a
 nd small\, in natural habitats.  Rendered in an impressionistic textured
  style\, these works imbue their subjects with a lively spirit.  Bald ea
 gles leave the viewer awed with their regal presence.  While the Steller
  and Scrub jays jauntily hint at their quirky character. In “Circling th
 e Light” the viewer joins a flock of geese on its migratory path. “Bir
 ds enliven our daily existence and their wild spirit provides endless subj
 ect matter\,” Bird noted of her inspiration for the series.\n\nMeet the 
 artist: Bird will host the Gallery on July 22 & 27\, 2:30 – 6pm and July
  29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday
 \, July 2\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of
  Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creativity with ov
 er 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art G
 allery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN 
 DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor furt
 her information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.
 net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:21+ Latin Summer Fest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T020000
UID:260610iU5pp_0GIkqdhlVYOCOr2Q
DESCRIPTION:**DATE: FRIDAY JULY 17TH**\n\n**TIME: 10:00PM-2:00AM**\n\n**DO
 ORS OPEN: 9:30PM**\n\n**NO ENTRY AFTER 11:30PM**\n\n**AGES 21+. VALID IDS 
 REQUIRED.**\n\nGet ready for a night full of music\, dancing\, and Latin v
 ibes. **Latin Summer Fest** is taking over **Victory House** and **Chuck
 ’s Bowling!**\n\nWe’ve got a stacked lineup with three DJs and two liv
 e bandas that will keep the party going all night long across three differ
 ent dance floors.\n\n**FEATURING**\n\n🎧 DJ Willie — Mixing Banda Rave
  Music\n\n🎧 DJ Brxndo & DJ C-Los — Mixing Reggaeton\, Cumbia\, Mereng
 ue\, & Latin Hits\n\n🎺 Special Guest Banda Ultimo Comando\n\n**🎺** H
 eadliner Banda Nueva Generacion\n\n**Venue Highlights:**\n\n**Victory Hous
 e** offers a full bar\, including an impressive selection of 24 taps. A la
 te-night food menu will be available. During our live events\, our restaur
 ant turns into the biggest dance floor in Santa Rosa. \n\n**Chuck’s Bow
 ling** features 16 lanes\, two more dance floors\, and another full bar to
  keep the drinks flowing. Enjoy discounted 5 frame bowling games throughou
 t the night!\n\n**Ticket Information:** General Admission: $30\n\nLimited 
 tickets available – only 500!  If we sell out ahead of time\, no ticket
 s will be available at the door.\n\n**Bottle Service Information:** With t
 he purchase of a bottle\, you receive a VIP table and two mixers of your c
 hoice. Inquire about bottle service at the door.\n\n**IMPORTANT EVENT POLI
 CIES:**\n\n**\\*Valid ID's Required** In order to consume alcoholic bevera
 ges\, you must establish that you are at least 21 years of age.\n\n**We ac
 cept the following Identification** for the purchase of alcohol per Alcoho
 l Beverage Control standards:\n\n\\- State issued driver license.\n\n\\- S
 tate Issued Identification card.\n\n\\- Passport or passport card.\n\n\\- 
 Military ID.\n\n**Legally acceptable identification** is one card that con
 tains these six characteristics:\n\n\\- Issued by a U.S. government agency
  (federal\, state\, county\, or city)\n\n\\- Name of the person\n\n\\- Dat
 e of birth\n\n\\- Photograph\n\n\\- Physical description (height\, weight\
 , hair\, and eye color)\n\n\\- Currently valid (not expired)\n\n**We do no
 t accept** the following forms of identification for the purchase of alcoh
 ol:\n\n\\- Foreign driver license/identification card\n\n\\- U.S. Governme
 nt Immigrant identification card\n\n\\- Birth Certificate\n\n\\- School or
  work identification card\n\n\\- Identification issued by a non-government
  agency\n\n\\- Social Security card\n\n\\- Interim or temporary driver lic
 ense or receipt for license from DMV\n\n\\- Check cashing card\n\n\\- Othe
 rwise valid document that is expired\, damaged\, altered\, borrowed\, stol
 en\, counterfeit\, or forged\n\n**\\*No bags allowed. Small handbags are a
 llowed but are subjected to search.**\n\n**\\*No smoking on the premises\,
  including vaporizers and electronic cigarettes.**\n\n**\\*No loitering. 
 Loitering on theses premises or in the adjacent parking areas is strictly 
 prohibited. If you are caught drinking in the parking lot you will be aske
 d to leave the premises.**\n\n**\\*No in-and-outs. Once you leave the even
 t you may not re-enter. This prevents unwanted activity from happening in 
 our parking lots.**\n\n**\\*No outside food and beverage is allowed inside
  of Poppy Bank Epicenter.** \n\n**Victory House**\n\n**3215 Coffey Ln\, S
 anta Rosa\, CA\, 95403**\n\n**info@visitepicenter.com**
LOCATION:Victory House
URL:https://www.sevenrooms.com/events/victoryhouse/evnnt
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
