DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T170000
UID:260313QbdUQj3r_ESYaSL_--BKzw
DESCRIPTION:***Spirit Guides: Fantastical Creatures from the Workshop of J
 acobo and María Ángeles*** features brightly colored\, richly patterned
  sculptures depicting imaginary hybrid animals that serve as spirit guides
  and astrological embodiments of human character. Inspired by the Zapotec 
 calendar\, the exhibition includes eight large-scale works organized by De
 nver Botanic Gardens.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Greg Lamboy Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T000000
UID:260312ji9ciGJy9EC7yNhLsvcPcA
DESCRIPTION:Greg Lamboy is a Northern California singer-songwriter whose p
 erformances combine lyrical honesty\, melodic craft\, and soulful acoustic
  guitar. Known for his confident yet comforting stage presence\, Greg weav
 es together original songs and reimagined favorites that invite listeners 
 to slow down and connect. His music blends strength and sensitivity\, reve
 aling deep emotion without pretense and reminding audiences why live music
  matters. Greg has released five albums and continues to captivate audienc
 es across the region\, both as a solo artist and as frontman for the Ameri
 cana band Pacific Standard.
LOCATION:Viansa Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107941816?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T140000
UID:260618jobjXdAXw06FE3pqJXONbA
DESCRIPTION:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village\n\nFree live
  music\, good vibes\, and a great excuse to make a Sunday out of it.\n\nSu
 mmer Sundays Music Series is a free monthly event bringing live music to t
 he Courtyard at Montgomery Village all summer long. This year\, we’re fe
 aturing local saxophonist Jimmy Galvan\, whose sound sets the perfect back
 drop for a relaxed afternoon in the heart of Sonoma County. Come for the m
 usic\, stay for the shopping\, dining\, coffee and ice cream. No tickets\,
  no fuss\, just a great community afternoon.\n\nJoin us on Sunday\, July 1
 9th from 12–2pm in the Courtyard at Montgomery Village (located near Mon
