BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Etching & Aquatint
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T140000
UID:2606273UI2zOv6EE2S_tYu6DmjTg
DESCRIPTION:Sundays · 2 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nJuly 12 & July 19\, 2026\
 n\n10:00 AM – 2:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking
 \n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration 
 Cost:\n\n$185\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$40\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$225
 \n\n**Aquatint and Multi-Plate Registration** Join our next two-session wo
 rkshop and study the art of copper plate etching! Open to new beginners or
  continuing students\, this unique course is focused on achieving the rich
  tones of aquatint and the precision of multi-plate registration. This is 
 your opportunity to learn a 500-year-old printmaking process with techniqu
 es favored by masters like Rembrandt\, Goya\, Picasso\, and Mary Cassatt. 
 In the first meeting\, you will learn (or review) how to prepare your copp
 er plate\, design your image\, apply a ground\, and then etch with a spray
  paint aquatint. Between sessions\, your instructor will carefully manage 
 the etching process by immersing your plate in the etchant solution. Durin
 g the second meeting\, you will learn to ink your plate(s)\, prepare paper
 \, and operate the printing press. You will also take part in a multi-plat
 e registration demonstration to incorporate various colors and layers into
  a single print. Upon completing this workshop\, you will have the skills 
 to create beautiful\, hand-pulled prints and take home your etched copper 
 plate\, ready for independent practice during printmaking open studio sess
 ions. This comprehensive course also covers essential knowledge of papers\
 , tools\, and inks.  Prior etching and print studio experience is helpful
 \, but not required. Continuing etching students are welcome to attend and
  continue working on prior etchings or create new plates. Students will re
 ceive instruction\, and can choose to work with the instructor to develop 
 projects based on their next level of learning. Interested participants ar
 e welcomed to contact the instructor for any questions about the workshop.
   ***This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the etching tools. Pa
 rticipants should feel comfortable using tools with sharp edges and using 
 printing equipment.***
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-etching-aqu
 atint/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guelaguetza Oaxaca Tierra del Sol
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T210000
UID:260626pfxaie5LF0uZKo7GuYE1jA
DESCRIPTION:¡Vive la magia y el encanto cultural de Oaxaca!\n\nLa organiz
 ación comunitaria *Oaxaca Tierra del Sol* invita con entusiasmo al festiv
 al Guelaguetza en el condado de Sonoma a festejar el 19 de julio de 2026. 
 En el marco de la gran fiesta familiar\, los asistentes podrán apreciar e
 l mosaico cultural del estado mexicano de Oaxaca.\n\nSerá un día mágico
  mientras se aprecia la sinfonía de la música filarmonica en vivo\, las 
 expresiones dancísticas y poéticas que aluden con fervor los distintos r
 incones de los pueblos de Oaxaca. Se presentarán la mayoría de las obras
  folclóricas más representativas del festival Guelaguetza.\n\nDurante la
  fiesta de hermandad\, se comparten los valores culturales y se muestra el
  rostro espiritual de los pueblos originarios y mestizos de Oaxaca\, Méxi
 co. Los asistentes podrán apreciar las bellas artes ejecutadas por artist
 as comunitarias provenientes de diferentes condados del estado de Californ
 ia. Además\, podrán adquirir algunas artesanías\, degustar de la rica c
 omida oaxaqueña y recabar información pertinente al bienestar comunitari
 o.\n\nEl festival Guelaguetza que se celebra en el Cerro del Fortín en la
  ciudad de Oaxaca\, es la fiesta étnica más grande de América Latina cu
 yas réplicas se extienden a varias ciudades de California y Estados Unido
 s.
LOCATION:Foley Family Community Pavillion
URL:https://www.facebook.com/Guelaguetza-Oaxaca-Tierra-del-Sol-10418787231
 0673
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
