BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Block Printed Beeswax Fabric Wraps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260723T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260723T203000
UID:260627YQJ0D1uzf0qWRrjMGS7lCA
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nThursday\, July 23\, 2026\n\n5:30 PM – 8:30 P
 M\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\, Summer at the Cente
 r\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistratio
 n Cost:\n\n$40\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n
 \n$40\n\nSpend a creative evening making a beautiful DIY printed eco-frien
 dly project!Learn to create sustainably responsible\, reusable block-print
 ed\, food safe beeswax fabric wraps as an alternative to using disposable 
 plastics. The DIY process involves carving a small potato block pattern\, 
 printing it onto 100% cotton\, then cutting the fabric and coating it with
  beeswax\, rosin\, and oil. This flexible\, sealable alternative to plasti
 c is a fun and inspiring hands-on project to make and use!You’ll design 
 and carve your own potato block\, then use it to print your own custom fab
 ric used for the functional beeswax wrap. Sip wine\, meet new people\, and
  enjoy a relaxed\, creative atmosphere as you learn the art of block print
 ing and eco-friendly crafting. Whether you come with friends or solo\, thi
 s workshop is the perfect way to unwind\, connect\, and leave with practic
 al handmade pieces you’ll be excited to use again and again. All printm
 aking materials and instructions are included — No experience is necessa
 ry. Just bring your creativity and curiosity!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/diy-block-printed-beeswax-f
 abric-wraps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
