BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T160000
UID:260629J2rNKATN2km8UIUchhjmuA
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Beginners Monday (Marin Salsa Class)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T200000
UID:260630iEHYiLyPM0y1mFRnQuEWGQ
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner Marin salsa class where no e
 xperience or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have 
 fun!\n\nGreat for first timers!\n\n• No dance experience required\n\n•
  Non-marking shoes soles\n\n• No partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed enviro
 nment is perfect for learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyab
 le. In this class you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame fo
 r partner-work and simple turn patterns.\n\nWe organize our curriculum so 
 that the movements are easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals
 ! No experience is necessary and no partner is required.\n\nDate & Time:\n
 \n• Mondays @ 7:00 PM – 8:00PM\n\n• Instructor: Lucie Ebnerova\n\n
 • Address: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 
 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
