BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ulysses Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T180000
UID:260630TCJgqjazeU6NLjoUEqzgfw
DESCRIPTION:Join us Monday evenings throughout June at The Sea Ranch Lodge
  for a community reading and discussion inspired by James Joyce’s Ulysse
 s. Part of the worldwide “Ulysses in 80” reading project\, these gathe
 rings connect local readers with a global community moving through the nov
 el together one day at a time.\n\nThe project is co-led by local resident 
 and writer Mark Sanford Gross alongside Dublin-based Joyce scholar Cliona 
 O’Farrelly of Trinity College Dublin. Local readers may also know Mark t
 hrough his storytelling project\, Write Up the Coast\, which focuses on co
 nversation\, connection\, and shared stories along the Mendocino and Sonom
 a Coast.\n\nDesigned to be welcoming\, conversational\, and open to all le
 vels of familiarity\, the evenings are not academic lectures or formal cla
 sses\, but a chance to gather\, reflect\, question\, laugh\, and share the
  experience of reading a famously complex and rewarding work alongside oth
 ers. First-time readers\, longtime Joyce enthusiasts\, and the simply curi
 ous are all encouraged to attend.\n\nEven if you are not actively reading 
 the book\, you are warmly welcome to join the conversation\, listen in\, a
 nd experience the spirit of the project: discovering how even the most cha
 llenging works of art become more approachable when explored together.\n\n
 More information and daily readings:\n\nulyssesin80.com\n\nQuestions or up
 dates:\n\nreadingulyssesin80@gmail.com
LOCATION:Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/ulysses-book-club/19304
 506/2026-07-27T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
